  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a refresh after a pinch zoom to reopen near the message I was reading, so that zooming does not make me lose my place.\n\n### Found by\nMac check of LOT-186 (#552) on dev-swift dc38ffb9, iPhone 18 Pro simulator (iOS 27.0), logged out, public topic (page 1).\n\n### Steps\n1. Open a topic, scroll 3 screens down.\n2. Pinch out (scale about 1.8). The same message stays at the top.\n3. Tap Actualiser, wait 8 s.\n\n### Expected\nThe page reopens at the same message (or very near).\n\n### Actual\nIt reopens several messages further down (about 1 h 45 of topic time later). Without zoom the same refresh lands exactly (0 pt shift, 5 samples over 14 s, plus a second refresh). Likely cause: the reading top is saved in zoomed viewport points and restored with window.scrollTo in layout points, so the zoom factor multiplies the offset (ReaderWebController+Scroll.swift, reader.js unchanged).\n\n### Suggested direction (not a fix)\nRestore through a message: the topmost post plus its distance to the bar's edge, landed with landOnPost (as noted on #552).\n\nRefs #545\n",
